halflife-idrive
===============

Half-Life (1998) on the BMW iDrive 7 (MGU) head unit: a native port on the Xash3D FWGS engine, installed through
the MGU Store. An unofficial project: not affiliated with or endorsed by Valve Corporation or BMW AG. Half-Life is
a trademark of Valve Corporation; BMW and iDrive are trademarks of BMW AG.

NO GAME DATA IS IN THIS REPOSITORY, and none is in anything built from it. Half-Life's maps, models, sounds and
textures belong to Valve. You need your own copy of the game; the head unit reads it from your USB stick.
BMW's app SDK is not in this repository either and may not be published; the MGU Store's build on the head unit
uses the unit's own.

This repository has parts under different licences:

  apps/clucraft_halflife/, tools/, test/, docs/, docker/, the files at the root     MIT (LICENSE)
  native/clucraft-halflife/                                                         GPL-3.0-or-later (its LICENSE; its NOTICE
                                                                                    lists what is in bin/)
  port/                                                                             GPL-3.0-or-later (port/LICENSE): this
                                                                                    project's changes to the engine
  kit/                                                                              MIT (kit/LICENSE.idrive7-apps, kit/LICENSE.nickgcode)

The app (MIT) and the service with the engine (GPL) are separate programs that talk over a socket.

